Z||000000||Smokin87||01-13-2001||02:34 PM||||the manual says to use a special antifreeze or you could ruin the engine.  is this true, and if so, what kind should i get.  also, what would happen if i used another antifreeze?||||reg||4
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-13-2001||04:38 PM||||engine coolant/antifreeze is all the same stuff more or less. just pick the brand you want and mix it 50% water and anti freeze before adding it to filler. You can add a can of 'water wetter' too at same time if you have any kind of running hot problems.it drops your coolant temp 10-15*||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-13-2001||05:44 PM||||You're Fiero manual says special coolant?  Or another one of your car's does.  First off, Fiero manual's say "this car requires a special coolant fill procedure"  That referrs to the proper "burping" of the coolant system when you drain/refill it; to get all the air bubbles out.  Newer cars today have extended lift coolant, which is pink...you can't mix regular ethylene glycol (green) antifreeze with the newer pink stuff.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
